# The settings of a parlor that Docker Compose runs (compose.yaml). setup.sh writes them to .env in
# /opt/parlornet, starting from this file. Each line that starts with # shows a setting with its default or an
# example. To change a setting, remove the # in front of it, give it a value and run
# "sudo systemctl restart parlornet". A value is plain text without quotes. A $ in a value starts a variable.
#
# The admin menus and the settings file (PARLOR_SETTINGS_FILE) can set the parlor's own settings too, and what
# they set wins over this file.

# ---- The parlor ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The server's name, shown in its greeting and in the mail it sends.
# PARLOR_NAME=parlornet

# How players sign in, none or password.
# PARLOR_AUTH=password

# How players sign up, none, password or email. With email, signing up mails the player a temporary password,
# and the parlor needs an SMTP relay in the settings file. The default goes with PARLOR_AUTH.
# PARLOR_SIGNUP=password

# The server extensions to start, separated by commas, until the admin menus choose them. By default every one
# starts.
# PARLOR_ADAPTERS=web,telnet,play,admin,bot

# The names the web site answers to, separated by commas. By default it answers to any name.
# PARLOR_WEB_HOSTS=games.example.org

# The web site's own address when an HTTPS proxy on the host serves it on the usual ports. Its pages then name
# that address as canonical. The proxy's address, as the container sees it, goes in PARLOR_WEB_PROXIES. For a
# proxy on the host, that is 172.30.4.1.
# PARLOR_WEB_URL=https://games.example.org/
# PARLOR_WEB_PROXIES=172.30.4.1

# The address players open for ParlorNet Play, through the HTTPS proxy, and the proxy's address as the
# container sees it. The web site's /play sends players to PARLOR_PLAY_URL.
# PARLOR_PLAY_URL=https://games.example.org/play/
# PARLOR_PLAY_PROXIES=172.30.4.1

# Your mailto: or https: address, which ParlorNet Play gives the browsers' push services. Play sends no push
# notifications without it and without PARLOR_PLAY_URL.
# PARLOR_PLAY_PUSH_CONTACT=mailto:ops@example.org

# The dial-in gateways' addresses as the container sees them, separated by commas. A gateway on the host comes
# from 172.30.4.1. The calls they carry to port 6521 have three time limits in minutes. One call has the first
# limit, one player's calls in a month have the second and all calls in a month together have the third. 0
# means no limit.
# PARLOR_DIALIN_GATEWAYS=172.30.4.1
# PARLOR_DIALIN_CALL_MINS=75
# PARLOR_DIALIN_USER_MONTH_MINS=60
# PARLOR_DIALIN_POOL_MONTH_MINS=150

# The same three limits for every other connection to port 6501. There are none by default.
# PARLOR_DEFAULT_CALL_MINS=0
# PARLOR_DEFAULT_USER_MONTH_MINS=0
# PARLOR_DEFAULT_POOL_MONTH_MINS=0

# The address that {contribute} in the message of the day shows, and the docs site that the web pages link
# to. If one of them is set to nothing, the line or the link is left out.
# PARLOR_CONTRIBUTE_URL=https://github.com/eric-cgn/parlornet
# PARLOR_DOCS_URL=http://docs.parlornet.org/

# ---- The container on this host -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The image to run. By default it is the release's image that compose.yaml names. For an image you built
# yourself with "docker build -t parlornet:local .", set it to parlornet:local.
# PARLOR_IMAGE=parlornet:local

# The host address that the players' ports are published on. By default they are on every address.
# PARLOR_PUBLISH_IP=192.0.2.10

# The host address that ParlorNet Play's port, 6513, is published on. By default it is the host's loopback
# address, for an HTTPS proxy on the host. Without a proxy, set it to the address in PARLOR_PUBLISH_IP, or
# set it to nothing to publish Play on every address.
# PARLOR_PLAY_PUBLISH=127.0.0.1

# The container's memory limit, and its limit on memory and swap together. By default the second one is
# Docker's own.
# PARLOR_MEMORY=448m
# PARLOR_MEMORY_SWAP=448m

# The players, the tables and the settings that the admin menus save live in this directory.
# PARLOR_DATA_DIR=/srv/parlornet

# This file holds settings you would rather keep out of .env, such as the SMTP relay's password. It is readable
# only by uid 10042.
# PARLOR_SETTINGS_FILE=/etc/parlornet/settings.conf

# The site's own files go in this directory. motd.txt is the message of the day, welcome.htm goes on the
# welcome page and pages/NAME.htm are pages of their own. Make the files readable by everyone.
# PARLOR_SITE_DIR=/srv/parlornet-site

# Server extensions on another host need deploy/install.sh and deploy/install-extensions.sh instead.
